<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Villers Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1146–1796</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Villers Abbey is a former Cistercian abbey near Villers-la-Ville in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walloon-brabant">Walloon Brabant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, founded in 1146 by monks sent from Clairvaux by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-of-clairvaux">Bernard of Clairvaux</a>. Richly endowed by the dukes of Brabant, it became one of the largest and most influential monasteries of the duchy. Suppressed in 1796, it is now one of the best-preserved Cistercian ruins in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/villers-abbey.jpg" alt="Villers Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abbaye de Villers-la-Ville asbl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_a%C3%A9rienne_de_l%27Abbaye_de_Villers-la-Ville.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
